## Where work belongs

Create, clone, and modify repositories under `{{ $machine.devRoot }}`. Keep
agent state inside the project's `./.local/`, never elsewhere in the home
directory.

{{ if $machine.features.ai -}}
## Agents on this machine

The agent CLIs (`claude`, `codex`, `omp`, `opencode`, `crush`, `kimi`, `grok`,
`cursor-agent`, and `agy`) are the **stock
upstream binaries** with their own authentication. Running one directly gives
you exactly the tool its vendor ships — no wrapper, no sandbox, no model
rewriting.

`ax` is a separate, opt-in launcher for `claude`, `codex`, `omp`, and
`opencode`. `ax <agent>` keeps the legacy sandbox-plus-gateway behavior;
`ax --sandbox <agent>` and `ax --gateway <agent>` select either boundary
independently. If you were launched through `ax`, a
further context section describes that boundary; if you do not see one, you are
running directly and none of it applies to you.

{{ end -}}
